   271 
   272 **Ledger.** Replace the two destination sets — `OutstandingNeeds`
   273 (`transfer_session/data_plane.rs:76`, created `mod.rs:3952`) and
   274 `GrantedHeaders` (`data_plane.rs:80`, `mod.rs:3953`), which today are both
   275 removed at claim (`mod.rs:4354-4367`, `data_plane.rs:2007-2011`) — with one
   276 `NeedLedger: HashMap<String, NeedState>` keyed by the exact header path:
   277 
   278 ```
   279 enum NeedState {
   280     Granted { header: FileHeader, resume: bool },   // need sent, nothing announced
   281     Active  { header, lane: Lane, kind: File | Resume },  // record announced on `lane`
   282     Completed,
   283     Failed,
   284 }
   285 enum Lane { Control, DataPlane }   // in-stream control stream vs the TCP socket
   286 ```
   287 
   288 Transitions, each a protocol violation if the current state does not
   289 allow it:
   290 
   291 | event (on lane L) | from | to | side effect |
   292 |---|---|---|---|
   293 | grant (need sent) | absent | Granted | — |
   294 | skip record for path | Granted | Failed | `record_failure(path, reason)` |
   295 | `FileBegin` / FILE tag / shard header member | Granted | Active(L) (shard members go straight to Completed on shard success, Failed on per-member containment as today) | sink `begin_record` → real writer, or a **discarding** writer carrying a contained destination failure (A16) |
   296 | terminator ok | Active(L), same L | Completed if the writer committed; Failed if it was discarding | sink `commit` (stamp, count, rename-over for staged records D-H); violation unless bytes == `header.size` |
   297 | terminator failed(reason) | Active(L), same L | Failed | sink `abort`; `record_failure` |
   298 | first `BlockTransfer` / BLOCK record | Granted(resume) | Active(L, Resume) | patch in place as today |
   299 | resume `BlockComplete` ok | Granted(resume) or Active(L, Resume), same L | Completed | stamp as today (zero-block case straight from the grant, A10) |
   300 | resume `BlockComplete` failed(reason) | Granted(resume) or Active(L, Resume), same L | Failed | leave partial unstamped; `record_failure` |
